  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "Given the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{12} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, find $\u2016144x\u2016.$",
  "worked_solution": "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n\u2016kx\u2016=|k|\\cdot \u2016x\u2016\n$$\n\nUsing this fact and the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016144x\u2016 & =|144|\u2016x\u2016 \\\\  & =144\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(\\sqrt{12})^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =144\\sqrt{64+4+12+1} \\\\  & =144\\sqrt{81} \\\\  & =144\\cdot 9 \\\\  & =1\\,296.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
